  "title": "Kontinuous Kontext: Instruction-Driven Image Editing with Scalar Edit Strength Control",
  "summary": "Kontinuous Kontext introduces a new dimension of control over edit strength in instruction-based image editing, allowing users to adjust edits gradually from subtle to strong across diverse operations like stylization, attribute, and material changes. This model extends a state-of-the-art image editing framework, enabling zero-shot adaptation through a lightweight projector network.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Kontinuous Kontext enables users to adjust edits gradually from no change to a fully realized result in a smooth and continuous manner.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "It uses a scalar edit strength input paired with an instruction to control the extent of the edit.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The model uses a lightweight projector network to map scalar input to coefficients in the model's modulation space.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
